-- title:
--   Hasse–Witt relation for point derivations on the Cartier dual
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal O$, with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbb Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel exactly $(p)$, and with $\mathcal O$ complete for the $(p)$-adic filtration. Let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal O$, i.e. a family $F_i \in \mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d,Y_1,\dots,Y_d]]$ with zero constant term, linear terms $X_i+Y_i$ and the associativity identity, assumed commutative. Let $v>0$, let $R$ be a commutative ring that is a Hopf algebra over $\mathcal O$, free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module, and let $\pi:\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to R$ be a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map such that each $\pi(X_i)$ lies in the radical of $(p)R$, such that $\pi$ is computed by $(p)$-adic evaluation at the elements $\pi(X_i)$, such that $\ker\pi$ is generated by the components of the $p^v$-fold iterate $[p^v]_F$ (defined recursively by $[0]_F=0$ and $[n+1]_F = F([n]_F,X)$), and such that the comultiplication satisfies $\Delta(\pi(X_i)) = F_i(\pi(X)\otimes 1, 1\otimes \pi(X))$, the right-hand side read as a $(p)$-adic evaluation in $R\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$. Then there are elements $D_1,\dots,D_d$ of the Cartier dual $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbb Z/p}(\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}R,\mathbb Z/p)$ such that $D_i(1\otimes\pi(X_j)) = \delta_{ij}$, each $D_i$ satisfies the counit-derivation rule $D_i(ab) = D_i(a)\varepsilon(b)+\varepsilon(a)D_i(b)$, and the $p$-th power of $D_i$ in the dual's ring structure equals $\sum_k \overline{B_{ik}}\,D_k$, where $B_{ik}\in\mathcal O$ is the coefficient of $X_i^{\,p}$ in the $k$-th component of $[p]_F$ and the bar denotes its image in $\mathbb Z/p$.
--
--   This identifies the invariant point derivations at the origin of the Hopf algebra of $F[p^v]$ modulo $p$ and computes their $p$-th convolution powers by the Hasse–Witt matrix of the multiplication-by-$p$ series of $F$, so that the restricted Lie algebra of the Cartier dual is described explicitly. It is used to deduce nilpotence of the Hasse–Witt matrix when the Cartier dual is local.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_exists_cartierDual_derivation_pow_eq_sum_hasseWitt_smul.lean

